Vesuvius Challenge Checklist: 
  NumPy: 
    understanding 2D and 3D arrays 
    can slice Volumetric data 
    know broadcasting 
    Normalising image arrays 
    Stacking slices into a 3D volume
    Extension: Processing arrays without Python loops 

  Pandas:
    Read and filter CSVs 
    Merge metadata 
    Convert between DataFrame and NumPy 

  Matplotlib: 
    Display CT slices 
    Plot Histograms 
    Compare graphs before and after pre-processing

  Images as Numerical Data 
    Knowledge of image data (2D arrays of numbers) 
    Pixel intensity (dark to light) 
    Grayscale vs RGB 
    image shapes (H,W) vs (H,W,C)
    Bit depth: 8-bit (0-255) and 16-bit (0-65535) [This is very important for CT scans) 
    Different file formats (PNG/JPG compressed and then TIFF (used heavily in Vesuvius)

Image Loading and Inspection: 
    How to load images with PIL, opencv-python and skimage.io 
    Checking: Shape, dtype and min/max values 
    Displaying images correctly (imshow, cmap = "gray")

Intensity Normalisation and Contrast:
  Different Normalisation Methods: Min-max scaling, Z-score normalisation, Histogram inspection, clipping outliers, contrast stretching
  Evaluating between global vs local normalisation 
